<%# A session whose turn has been handed over and is sitting in GoodJob's `agents`
    lane waiting for one of its worker threads.

    Before #1040 this session read `running` and needed no banner, because the
    status itself was the (false) explanation. Now it reads `waiting` — which is
    the truth, and which is also what a spot hold, a ceiling pause, an auth-outage
    park and an ordinary sleep read. Without a line saying which of those it is, a
    session about to run looks exactly like one nobody is coming for.

    Gated on SessionWaitingReason's ranking rather than on the job row directly,
    so this box and `get_session` cannot name different mechanisms — and so a
    session that is ALSO carrying an older hold or park shows the box for whichever
    of them is actually why it is waiting. %>
<%# The caller passes the ranking in when it has already computed one for the
    spot banner beside this one, so a session page asks `good_jobs` once rather
    than once per banner per breakpoint. %>
<% waiting_reason = local_assigns.fetch(:waiting_reason) { SessionWaitingReason.for(agent_session) } %>
<% queued = waiting_reason&.current %>
<% if queued&.key == SessionWaitingReason::TURN_QUEUED %>
  <%# A data attribute rather than an id: this partial renders twice per page —
      once in the mobile block, once in the desktop header — and two elements
      cannot share one id. %>
  <div class="mb-4 rounded-md border border-sky-200 bg-sky-50 p-4" data-queued-turn-banner>
    <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-sky-500 shrink-0 mt-0.5" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
        <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm1-11a1 1 0 10-2 0v4a1 1 0 00.293.707l2 2a1 1 0 001.414-1.414L11 10.586V7z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
      </svg>
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-sky-900">
          Queued for a worker
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-sky-800">
          This session has been handed a turn and is waiting for
          <span class="font-medium"><%= queued.label %></span>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-sky-700">
          Nothing is stuck and nobody needs to act. Zimmer runs
          <span class="font-medium"><%= RunningTurns.worker_slots %></span>
          agent turns at once, and this one starts as soon as a thread frees up.
          <span class="font-medium">Running</span> means a worker is executing a turn, so a
          session queued behind the pool reads <span class="font-medium">Waiting</span>.
        </p>
        <%# "Start mine now", and the whole of what it costs.

            This is the only lever that is about the POOL. Promoting the session
            to priority moves it past the spot gate, which is a different
            mechanism and holds nothing here; "Start it now" moves a turn that is
            scheduled for later, and this turn is already due. The only way to get
            a thread is to take one.

            Computed here rather than threaded in from the caller because the
            partial is only reached for a session that is genuinely queued, which
            is a small population — and because the button's two claims (the pool
            is full, and THIS is the turn that would be stopped) have to come from
            one snapshot. See Sessions::ForceTurnStart. %>
        <% force = Sessions::ForceTurnStart.preview(agent_session) %>
        <% if force&.available? %>
          <%# The victim by name and by age, before the click rather than after
              it. Zimmer cannot tell what another session is in the middle of —
              there is no signal on a session row for "half-way through an
              irreversible external action" — so the confirmation hands the
              person the two facts it does have and leaves the judgement to them. %>
          <% victim = force.victim %>
          <% age = force.victim_age ? "#{distance_of_time_in_words(force.victim_age)} ago" : "an unknown time ago" %>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-sky-700" data-queued-turn-force-cost>
            All <%= RunningTurns.worker_slots %> threads are busy. <span class="font-medium">Force</span>
            takes one by stopping the turn that started most recently —
            <%= link_to "session ##{victim.id}", session_path(victim), class: "font-medium underline" %>,
            <%= victim.priority_class %>, started <%= age %>. That turn is not cancelled: it is put
            straight back in the queue and runs again as soon as a thread frees up. What it loses is
            the tool call it is in the middle of.
          </p>
          <%# The previewed victim rides along, so the session that dies is the one
              the person confirmed: a pick that differs at the click is refused
              rather than quietly stopping the next one down. %>
          <%= button_to "Force",
                force_start_session_path(agent_session),
                method: :post,
                params: { expected_victim_id: victim.id },
                form: {
                  class: "mt-2",
                  data: {
                    turbo_confirm: "Stop session ##{victim.id}'s turn (#{victim.priority_class}, " \
                      "started #{age}) to free a worker thread for session ##{agent_session.id}?\n\n" \
                      "Its work on disk survives and its turn goes back in the queue, but the tool " \
                      "call it is in the middle of is lost — and Zimmer cannot tell what that is."
                  }
                },
                class: "inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-sky-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-sky-900 shadow-sm hover:bg-sky-100 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-sky-500 focus:ring-offset-1" %>
        <% elsif force %>
          <%# No button rather than a button that does nothing. The sentence is the
              service's own, so the page and the flash a click would have produced
              say the same thing. %>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-sky-700" data-queued-turn-force-unavailable>
            <%= force.message %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
